       "text": {
        "characters": "You are invited to take part in research evaluating the iSupport-D digital support program for carers of people living with dementia.\r\nParticipation may involve:\r\nCompleting questionnaires or feedback activities\r\nAllowing analysis of how you use the platform\r\nContributing information about caregiving experiences and wellbeing\r\nSome questions may relate to health or other sensitive personal information.\r\nYour participation is voluntary.\r\nBefore agreeing, please understand that:\r\nYou may decline to answer any question.\nYou may withdraw from research participation at any time without penalty.\nWithdrawal will not affect access to general educational program content unless required by the research protocol.\r\nInformation collected may be analysed in de-identified or aggregated form and used in research publications or reports.\nIdentifiable data will be handled securely in accordance with privacy laws and ethics approval.\r\nYour data may be stored or analysed by authorised research partners, including those located outside Australia.\r\nThe platform uses digital analytics and AI-enabled tools to improve program delivery. These tools do not provide medical diagnosis or treatment advice.\r\nIf you have concerns about the conduct of this research, you may contact the approving Human Research Ethics Committee.",
